desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "JavaScript Debugger"
	title_zh: "JavaScript Debugger"
	type: audit
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-best-practice-javascript-debugger"
	risk: "Best Practice"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `javascript-debugger` (javascript/lang/best-practice/leftover_debugging.yaml).
Original message: found debugger call; should this be in production code?
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.js": <<<POS
debugger;
POS
	"safefile://pos.js": <<<NEG
console.log
NEG
)

${*.js}.pattern_regex(/(?:debugger;)/) as $p0
${*.ts}.pattern_regex(/(?:debugger;)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "JavaScript Debugger",
	title_zh: "JavaScript Debugger",
	message: "JavaScript Debugger detected.",
}
